## event-loop delay (monitorEventLoopDelay, 10 ms resolution)
  a tick is synchronous, so it blocks the sampler while it runs: max is the stall.
  every sample includes the sampler's own 10 ms period, so an idle loop reads about 10 ms:
  subtract the resolution before comparing a max against a phase's wall time.
  mean sits near that floor whenever the phase is short next to the 50 ms settle window.
